/.net-in-my-browser /net-in-my-browser/
/.net-in-my-browser/ /net-in-my-browser/

# gatsby-plugin-sitemap 6 renamed its output: one sitemap.xml became
# sitemap-index.xml plus sitemap-0.xml. Keep the long-published URL alive.
/sitemap.xml /sitemap-index.xml 301!
/tech-blog/sitemap.xml /sitemap-index.xml 301!

/tech-blog/admin/* /admin/:splat 301!
/tech-blog/admin/ /admin/ 301!
/tech-blog/admin /admin/ 301!
/tech-blog/a /admin/ 301!

https://tech.boldare.com/tech-blog/* https://boldare.com/tech-blog/:splat 301
https://tech.boldare.com/ https://boldare.com/tech-blog/ 301

# Gatsby's pathPrefix ("/tech-blog") is baked into every page/asset URL, but the
# build output itself is written unprefixed. Rewrite so this site is directly
# browsable (e.g. Netlify deploy previews) without a fronting proxy.
# Scoped to path only (no host), so it only ever applies on hosts not already
# matched above (tech.boldare.com is redirected away by the rules before this).
/tech-blog/* /:splat 200
